# Franklin Voter Guide, November 2026. Every person, place, party, and measure in this file is
# fictional. It exists to exercise every construct of the Oval format at the scale of a real
# metropolitan guide: six root ballots, forty-four contests, twenty-eight measures.

oval 0.1

guide "Franklin Voter Guide"
election "November 3, 2026 General Election"
date 2026-11-03

note:
  Written by the Franklin Civic Alliance. We interviewed every candidate who agreed to meet with
  us and read every measure in full. Where a board member had a conflict, they did not
  participate in that recommendation and we say so in the contest.

  Always double check the options printed on your own ballot.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- parties

party @dem "Democratic"
  abbreviation "D"
party @gop "Republican"
  abbreviation "R"
party @green "Green"
  abbreviation "G"
party @lib "Libertarian"
  abbreviation "LIB"
party @pf "Peace and Freedom"
  abbreviation "PF"

# ------------------------------------------------------------- candidates
# Only people who appear in more than one contest.

candidate @dana-lombardi "Dana Lombardi"
  designation "United States Senator"
  party @dem
  note:
    Appointed in January 2025 to fill the vacancy left by Senator Hale's resignation. Previously
    Secretary of State of Franklin.
candidate @sofia-yilmaz "Sofia Yilmaz"
  designation "Business Owner"
  party @gop

# ======================================================================
ballot @federal "Federal Government"

  section "Executive Offices"

    contest @president "President and Vice President of the United States" single
      subtitle "Vote for one ticket"
      note:
        The president and vice president run as a ticket. Your single vote elects both.

      campaign incumbent
        @hana-nakamura "Hana Nakamura" as "President"
          party @dem
        @hiro-eriksen "Hiro Eriksen" as "Vice President"
          party @dem
        website https://hananakamura2026.example
      campaign
        @yara-bergstrom "Yara Bergstrom" as "President"
          party @gop
        @omar-rowe "Omar Rowe" as "Vice President"
          party @gop
        website https://yarabergstrom2026.example
      campaign
        @victor-bergstrom "Victor Bergstrom" as "President"
          party @green
        @vera-mendez "Vera Mendez" as "Vice President"
          party @green
      campaign
        @petra-patel "Petra Patel" as "President"
          party @lib
        @samir-osei "Samir Osei" as "Vice President"
          party @lib
      campaign
        @petra-dominguez "Petra Dominguez" as "President"
          party @pf
        @quinn-guerrero "Quinn Guerrero" as "Vice President"
          party @pf
      campaign
        @ada-fontaine "Ada Fontaine" as "President"
          party @ind "Independence"
            abbreviation "IND"
        @camila-oyelaran "Camila Oyelaran" as "Vice President"
          party @ind

      recommend
        support @hana-nakamura
        justification:
          Hana Nakamura's first term delivered the port funding Franklin has sought for a
          decade. The challengers have not released a platform beyond a pledge to cut waste.

  section "United States Senate"

    contest @us-senate-special "United States Senator (Special Election)" single
      subtitle "Unexpired term ending January 3, 2027"
      tabulation "Plurality wins"
      note:
        This is the first of two Senate contests on your ballot. This one decides who holds the
        seat for the final weeks of the current term. Vote in both.

      campaign incumbent @dana-lombardi
      campaign @sofia-yilmaz

      recommend
        support @dana-lombardi
        justification:
          See the full-term contest below. Our reasoning is the same, and splitting the vote
          between the two contests would serve no purpose.

    contest @us-senate-full "United States Senator" single
      subtitle "Full term beginning January 3, 2027"
      tabulation "Plurality wins"

      campaign incumbent @dana-lombardi
      campaign @sofia-yilmaz
      campaign @kiran-thorne "Kiran Thorne"
        designation "Nurse"
        party @green

      recommend
        support @dana-lombardi
        justification:
          Dana Lombardi has used two years in the Senate to deliver the port funding Franklin
          has sought for a decade. Sofia Yilmaz has not held office.

  section "United States House of Representatives"

    contest @us-house-16 "United States Representative, District 16" single
      subtitle "Millbrook"

      campaign @quinn-okafor "Quinn Okafor"
        designation "Union Representative"
        party @dem
        website https://quinnokafor.example
      campaign @talia-jensen "Talia Jensen"
        designation "Civil Engineer"
        party @gop

      recommend
        support @quinn-okafor
        justification:
          This is a close call. Quinn Okafor and Talia Jensen agree on most of the substance;
          Quinn Okafor has the better track record of working across the aisle, which this seat
          needs.

    contest @us-house-12 "United States Representative, District 12" single
      subtitle "Brookhaven Hills"

      campaign @odalys-halvorsen "Odalys Halvorsen"
        designation "Transit Planner"
        party @dem
        website https://odalyshalvorsen.example
      campaign @marcus-ndiaye "Marcus Ndiaye"
        designation "Environmental Scientist"
        party @gop

      recommend
        support @odalys-halvorsen
        justification:
          Odalys Halvorsen ran the department that this office oversees and left it in better
          shape than they found it.

    contest @us-house-11 "United States Representative, District 11" single
      subtitle "Ashford"

      campaign incumbent @bram-mendez "Bram Mendez"
        designation "Farmer"
        party @dem
        website https://brammendez.example
      campaign @maeve-haddad "Maeve Haddad"
        designation "Farmer"
        party @gop

      recommend
        support @bram-mendez
        justification:
          Bram Mendez is the only candidate who answered our questionnaire in full. The others
          declined to meet with us.

