  section "Judicial"

    contest @supreme-court-retention "Supreme Court Justice" retention
      subtitle "Shall Justice Elena Villanueva be retained in office?"
      tabulation "Majority yes to retain"

      campaign incumbent @elena-villanueva "Elena Villanueva"
        designation "Justice of the Supreme Court"

      recommend
        support @elena-villanueva
        justification:
          Retention elections are not the place to relitigate a single decision. The bar
          evaluation is "well qualified" and the opinions are careful.

  section "Statewide Propositions"
    note:
      Propositions 2 through 6 were placed by the legislature. Propositions 32 through 36 are
      citizen initiatives.

    measure @prop-2 "Proposition 2"
      subtitle "Public school facilities bond"
      description:
        Shall the measure titled "Public school facilities bond" be adopted, authorizing the
        actions described in the full text and amending the relevant code sections accordingly?
      if_yes:
        The public school facilities bond would take effect as described.
      if_no:
        Current law would remain unchanged.
      placement "Citizen initiative (signature petition)"
      tabulation "Simple majority"
      fiscal_impact "$300 per parcel per year for 30 years"
      supporters "Franklin Small Business Network", "Franklin Police Officers Association", "Riders United"
      opponents "Franklin Realtors Association", "Riders United"

      recommend yes
        justification:
          The existing subsidy is not enough and this modest increase is a cheap fix. It will
          not solve the underlying shortage, but it is better than nothing.

    measure @prop-3 "Proposition 3"
      subtitle "Right to marry"
      placement "Veto referendum"
      tabulation "Majority of all registered voters"
      fiscal_impact "$96 per parcel per year for 15 years"
      supporters "Transit Riders Alliance", "Riders United"
      opponents none

      recommend yes
        justification:
          This is a straightforward bond for infrastructure the district has deferred for a
          decade. The repayment schedule is conservative and the oversight committee has real
          teeth.

    measure @prop-4 "Proposition 4"
      subtitle "Climate and wildfire bond"
      description:
        Shall the measure titled "Climate and wildfire bond" be adopted, authorizing the actions
        described in the full text and amending the relevant code sections accordingly?
      if_yes:
        The climate and wildfire bond would take effect as described.
      if_no:
        Current law would remain unchanged.
      placement "Legislative referral"
      tabulation "Requires 55%"
      fiscal_impact "About $96 million a year in new revenue"

      recommend yes
        justification:
          Two of our board members work for organizations that would receive funding under this
          measure. They recused themselves and the remaining members were evenly split.

    measure @prop-5 "Proposition 5"
      subtitle "55% threshold for local housing bonds"
      placement "Citizen initiative (signature petition)"
      tabulation "Requires two-thirds of votes cast"
      supporters "Sierra Club, Franklin Chapter", "Franklin Small Business Network", "Franklin Police Officers Association"
      opponents "Franklin Nurses Union", "Franklin Teachers Association"

      recommend yes
        justification:
          The existing subsidy is not enough and this modest increase is a cheap fix. It will
          not solve the underlying shortage, but it is better than nothing.

    measure @prop-6 "Proposition 6"
      subtitle "End involuntary servitude in prisons"
      description:
        Shall the measure titled "End involuntary servitude in prisons" be adopted, authorizing
        the actions described in the full text and amending the relevant code sections
        accordingly?
      if_yes:
        The end involuntary servitude in prisons would take effect as described.
      if_no:
        Current law would remain unchanged.
      placement "Placed by the District Board"
      tabulation "Simple majority"
      fiscal_impact "No direct fiscal effect"
      supporters "Sierra Club, Franklin Chapter"
      opponents none

      recommend yes
        justification:
          The existing subsidy is not enough and this modest increase is a cheap fix. It will
          not solve the underlying shortage, but it is better than nothing.

    measure @prop-32 "Proposition 32"
      subtitle "$18 minimum wage"
      placement "Placed by the City Council"
      tabulation "Majority of all registered voters"
      fiscal_impact "Authorizes $96 million in bonds, repaid by property taxes over 30 years"

      recommend no-position
        justification:
          The mechanism here is the problem, not the goal. It sets no limits on what localities
          may do in its place, and the cities most eager to use it have the worst records on the
          underlying issue.

          We would support a narrower version. Vote no on this one.

    measure @prop-33 "Proposition 33"
      subtitle "Repeal state rent-control preemption"
      description:
        Shall the measure titled "Repeal state rent-control preemption" be adopted, authorizing
        the actions described in the full text and amending the relevant code sections
        accordingly?
      if_yes:
        The repeal state rent-control preemption would take effect as described.
      if_no:
        Current law would remain unchanged.
      placement "Placed by the District Board"
      tabulation "Requires two-thirds of votes cast"
      fiscal_impact "$48 per parcel per year for 10 years"
      supporters "Millbrook Neighborhood Council"
      opponents "League of Women Voters of Franklin", "Sierra Club, Franklin Chapter"

      recommend no
        justification:
          This is a straightforward bond for infrastructure the district has deferred for a
          decade. The repayment schedule is conservative and the oversight committee has real
          teeth.

    measure @prop-34 "Proposition 34"
      subtitle "Restrict spending of prescription drug revenue"
      placement "Legislative referral"
      tabulation "Simple majority"
      supporters "Brookhaven Tenants Union", "Franklin Police Officers Association"
      opponents none

      recommend yes
        justification:
          The mechanism here is the problem, not the goal. It sets no limits on what localities
          may do in its place, and the cities most eager to use it have the worst records on the
          underlying issue.

          We would support a narrower version. Vote no on this one.

    measure @prop-35 "Proposition 35"
      subtitle "Permanent managed care tax"
      description:
        Shall the measure titled "Permanent managed care tax" be adopted, authorizing the
        actions described in the full text and amending the relevant code sections accordingly?
      if_yes:
        The permanent managed care tax would take effect as described.
      if_no:
        Current law would remain unchanged.
      placement "Required by the City Charter"
      tabulation "Requires 55%"
      fiscal_impact "Authorizes $12 million in bonds, repaid by property taxes over 10 years"

      recommend yes
        justification:
          The existing subsidy is not enough and this modest increase is a cheap fix. It will
          not solve the underlying shortage, but it is better than nothing.

    measure @prop-36 "Proposition 36"
      subtitle "Felony charges for certain drug and theft crimes"
      placement "Placed by the City Council"
      tabulation "Requires two-thirds of votes cast"
      fiscal_impact "Authorizes $12 million in bonds, repaid by property taxes over 20 years"
      supporters "Brookhaven Tenants Union", "Franklin Small Business Network", "Franklin Nurses Union"
      opponents "Millbrook Neighborhood Council", "Franklin Small Business Network"

      recommend no
        justification:
          Enshrines in the charter a right the courts have already recognized. Cheap, symbolic,
          and worth doing.

